Revision history of Archive-Tree


0.00_00  2026-11-20  RC
    + dirc compiles a specification (the file named, or
      standard input) to mtree(5), on standard output or -o.
      It takes -C, -h and -V as siteconf does.
    + RdKw::Archive::Tree describes the specification.
    + RdKw::Archive::Tree::Reader reads it.  The string and byte
      string escapes are those of trivnote libexpr 0.2.0, except
      that an escape without braces takes no spaces, `-' or `_'
      between its digits, and needs at least one digit.
    + RdKw::Archive::Tree::MTree writes mtree(5): names spelled by
      to_fs, with \ooo for bytes that are not plain ASCII.
      It reads ISO 8601 times with Time::Piece.
    + dirc-git writes a Git tree, or paths in it, as a tar archive
      (-z: gzip), with the bytes git archive writes for the same
      umask and time.  It takes --uid and --gid as name:id, --mtime,
      --umask, --fmask, --dmask and --prefix.  A `.' in a path
      says where the names in the archive start.
    + RdKw::Archive::Ustar writes ustar with pax headers, laid out
      as git archive lays them out.
    + RdKw::DVCS::Git::Tar reads the tree with git ls-tree and
      cat-file, and export-ignore with git check-attr --source.
